WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.380
Today's 'Drew Gooder' is Sherina Jones

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.910
from Miami, Florida, who's making headlines

3
00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.800
for her organization Village (FREE)DGE.

4
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.100
And she came up with a unique way to provide free meals

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.150
to Miami locals who have been struggling

6
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.700
through the pandemic.

7
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.820
And Sherina is here now.

8
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:18.780
I can't wait to meet her.

9
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.330
Hello.

10
00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.046
Hi Drew, thank you so much for having me.

11
00:00:22.046 --> 00:00:24.490
(audience clapping)

12
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:29.490
Oh my gosh Sherina, you're so beautiful inside and out.

13
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.670
Thank you.

14
00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:33.900
I was so excited about this story

15
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.910
because when the pandemic first started

16
00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:41.150
it was one of the things that I gravitated to most

17
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.240
was Community (Free)dges

18
00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:44.930
And yours is very special.

19
00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:47.603
Please tell us about it and when it started.

20
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.100
Village Free(dges) was founded in August of 2020.

21
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.054 line:15%
The word Free(dge) is a combination

22
00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:57.060 line:15%
of the word fridge and free.

23
00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.300 line:15%
I wanted to combat the growing hunger,

24
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.430
the crisis in the community

25
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.760
because the pandemic had taken a toll on so many families.

26
00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:07.790
So I just sat day and night, like what could I do to help?

27
00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.580 line:15%
So I took $180 of my own money

28
00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.340 line:15%
and I purchased the first community refrigerator.

29
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.740 line:15%
And I got with business owners, my cousin,

30
00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:18.750
Isaiah Thomas and Danny Agnew of Roots Collective.

31
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:22.250
And I asked them what they mind if I put a refrigerator

32
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:25.750
outside of their business and they agreed to do so.

33
00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:28.410
So that's how this amazing initiative started

34
00:01:28.410 --> 00:01:31.120
with two guys that agreed to put the refrigerator

35
00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.360
outside their business.

36
00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:34.180
And you also have a small business

37
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:37.160
that was impacted by the pandemic, right?

38
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.340
Yes, I am a full-time aesthetician, a Snob Beauty Box

39
00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.330
which is my baby that I birthed eight years ago.

40
00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:47.520 line:15%
So I do beauty services on women,

41
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.810 line:15%
eye lashes, makeup, skincare, and body waxing.

42
00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.180 line:15%
So in my remaining time outside

43
00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:57.400 line:15%
of running my full-time entrepreneurship job,

44
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.700
I take care of the community refrigerators.

45
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.770 line:15%
I mean, well so many of us wanna try

46
00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.510 line:15%
to figure out what we can do.

47
00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.350 line:15%
You are out there doing it.

48
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:12.403
What do you try to put in your (FREE)DGES, may I ask.

49
00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.800
Inside of the refrigerators,

50
00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.760
we make sure we include water, canned goods,

51
00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:19.470
sandwiches, bread, potatoes, frozen foods

52
00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.863
that can be microwaved.

53
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.140
And we just don't accept anything that's opened

54
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.080
or half eaten and always be sure to check the dates

55
00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.010
of things that are donated to the (FREE)DGE.

56
00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.600
I mean, it just seems like in everything you do

57
00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.930
whether it's your beautiful business as an aesthetician

58
00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.907
or building your community Free(dges),

59
00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:41.080
you're such a caretaker and so thoughtful

60
00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.160
and thorough about everything you're saying.

61
00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:47.520
And Drew Gooders like you, are just so important

62
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.490
to us here at the show but far more importantly,

63
00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.430
the communities that they serve.

64
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.440
And we just wanted to tell you

65
00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.930 line:15%
that our friends at Omaha Steaks heard

66
00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.360 line:15%
about what you're doing

67
00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:02.260 line:15%
and they wanna send you $10,000

68
00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.906
worth of single serve protein meals and steak stacks.

69
00:03:06.906 --> 00:03:10.218
(audience cheering)

70
00:03:10.218 --> 00:03:11.885
Thank you so much.

71
00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.840
Sherina, you are such an inspiration.

72
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.740
I really mean it, when we sit there

73
00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:22.410
and we think about all the things we can do.

74
00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.240
I think the acting on it is the big difference

75
00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.160
and the way that you follow through,

76
00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.250
the example that you set

77
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:34.040
and the service and goodness and life-changing health

78
00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.813
that you provide people,

79
00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.940
were just on view here.

80
00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.500
Really, thank you.

81
00:03:41.476 --> 00:03:43.420
Thank you so much for having me.

82
00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:44.530
Thank you to Sherina.
Thank you.

83
00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:46.670
Okay, so for more information on how

84
00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.840 line:15%
you can help support the GoFundMe

85
00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.440 line:15%
for Village (FREE)DGE, (FREE)DGE

86
00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.690
visit our website and we'd love to drive as much support

87
00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.360
as we can to you Sherina.

88
00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.029
Thank you for everything you're doing.

89
00:04:00.029 --> 00:04:00.862
